From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: leds: backlight: pwm-backlight: Add max-duty-cycle-percent

Some front lights must not be driven at a full duty cycle: the vendor
driver of the Minimal Phone MP01's white front light never goes past a
quarter of the PWM period. Let the board say so.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/leds/backlight/pwm-backlight.yaml | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/backlight/pwm-backlight.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/backlight/pwm-backlight.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/backlight/pwm-backlight.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/backlight/pwm-backlight.yaml
@@ -49,6 +49,15 @@
       having to list out every possible value in the brightness-level array.
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
 
+  max-duty-cycle-percent:
+    description:
+      The duty cycle the highest brightness gives, for a light that must not
+      be driven harder than a fraction of the PWM period. Lower levels scale
+      down from it. Without it the highest level gives a 100% duty cycle.
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
+    minimum: 1
+    maximum: 100
+
 dependencies:
   default-brightness-level: [brightness-levels]
   num-interpolated-steps: [brightness-levels]
-- 
